From 3ef3e1df19e26995cb4df617be8abd164282259e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 1aeo <github@1aeo.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 08:45:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 08/20] relay_metrics: Add a gauge of tunneled directory server
 connections

Each BEGIN_DIR stream holds a linked exit and directory connection pair
with no socket, so tor_relay_connections doesn't count them, and nothing
else shows how many a relay holds or what they are doing. During a
BEGIN_DIR flood they can pile up in the connection array, and the cost
of walking it grows with them.

Add the gauge tor_relay_begindir_connections{state=...}, filled at
scrape time in one pass over the connection array. Each open BEGIN_DIR
stream is in exactly one state: its directory connection is waiting for
a request ("command_wait"), writing an onion service descriptor
("writing_hs_descriptor") or anything else ("writing_other"), or it is
gone and only the stream is left, draining onto the circuit
("draining"). Direct (DirPort) connections are not counted.

Part of #41339.
